This Privacy Policy explains how Chokas PMD collects, uses, shares, and protects information when using the internal application that integrates with QuickBooks Online (the “App”).

1) Scope

This Policy applies to:

Chokas PMD Authorized Users of the App; and

Personal information of individuals (customers, tenants, vendors, employees, subcontractors) that may be contained in business records processed through the App.

2) Data principles (QuickBooks platform expectations)

We:

Clearly define the purposes for using QuickBooks/customer data and use it only for those purposes.

Do not share one party’s data with another party unless explicitly stated and authorized.

Maintain privacy and security practices consistent with applicable laws and requirements.

3) Information we process
A) QuickBooks Online data (via Intuit APIs)

Depending on enabled permissions and features, the App may access/process:

Customers/tenants, vendors, employees (names, contact info, addresses as stored)

Invoices, bills, payments, deposits, expenses, purchase orders

Chart of accounts, classes/locations/projects, transactions, reports

Attachments if your workflows pull them (e.g., invoice PDFs)

B) App operational data

User identity (name/email/role) for access control

Audit logs (login events, key actions, timestamps)

Technical logs (device/browser metadata, IP address, error diagnostics)

C) Data you upload or enter

If the App supports uploads/notes, we process what Authorized Users provide (e.g., invoice references, project tags).

4) Purposes of processing

We use information to:

Run internal accounting and operations (invoice handling, job costing, vendor/customer management, reporting)

Sync authorized data with QuickBooks Online

Maintain security, access control, and auditability

Troubleshoot and improve reliability

Comply with legal obligations

5) How we share information

We may share information only with:

Internal recipients at Chokas PMD who need it for business operations (role-based access)

Service providers (e.g., hosting, monitoring, logging) under confidentiality/security obligations

Intuit/QuickBooks Online as required for API integration

Legal/regulatory recipients when required by law

We do not sell personal information or QuickBooks data.

No cross-customer sharing: This App is internal-only for Chokas PMD; it is not a multi-tenant product and does not share data across unrelated customer accounts.

6) Data retention

We retain information only as long as needed for the purposes above.

Set your policy to match your reality; pick one approach and delete the other:

Option A (recommended for internal integrations): Minimal persistence

We do not store full QuickBooks datasets long-term; we store only:

OAuth tokens/connection identifiers,

necessary mapping keys (e.g., QuickBooks entity IDs),

operational logs for [e.g., 90–365 days].

Option B (if you replicate QuickBooks data for analytics):

We store synchronized data in a secure database for [e.g., 24 months / 7 years] to support reporting, audits, and operational history.

Deletion/Disconnect

When a QuickBooks connection is disabled, we stop access immediately and delete or de-identify stored connection data within [e.g., 30 days], unless retention is required for legal/audit reasons.

7) Security controls

We use commercially reasonable safeguards designed to protect information, including access controls and logging. Intuit requires developers to maintain privacy/security practices and can verify compliance through audits/testing.

8) Authorized user responsibilities

Authorized Users must:

Use the App only for company business

Protect credentials and devices

Avoid exporting data to unapproved locations

Report suspected incidents promptly

9) Your rights and inquiries

If you are an employee/contractor and have questions about access, logs, or retention, contact us. If you are a customer/vendor/tenant whose data may appear in our records, you may request access/correction consistent with applicable law and our obligations.

10) Changes to this Policy

We may update this Policy and will post the updated version on our website. We maintain accurate records of our privacy and security practices as required.

